# CONCORD off against the four teams it lost to on both of its cards (TMODE-34, BENCH-160). Team
# thread: team-only, duel and melee fixtures bit for bit. CONCORD ships on every team (PR #496) and
# its fresh-seed confirm passed at +0.50 +- 0.43 APS (PR #529), but four teams read worse with it on
# both cards (pc-team-concord 12 seeds, then pc-team-concord2 16 fresh seeds, share points):
# OgiTeam -3.8 then -9.5 +- 3.4, NightmareTeam -1.1 then -8.6 +- 4.0, FirestarterTeam -1.9 then
# -4.8 +- 4.7, CombatTeam -1.6 then -3.9 +- 5.0. They were picked after the fact, so this card
# confirms them on fresh seeds before any table entry ships, as pc-team-nododge did for DODGE.
#   ncprep  build aa, bb, and xc: tmtab with plans/team-noconcord-table.java (Ogi, Combat and
#           Firestarter get MATEFIRE, HUNT, PATH and DODGE; Nightmare's two classes keep their shipped
#           MATEFIRE, HUNT and PATH: every mode they play today but CONCORD)
#   ncbb    bb vs aa, the 4 teams x 24 fresh seeds (base 7000), 10 rounds as the concord cards; ncxc the same for xc
#   ncsum   projected team APS change = (sum of each team's xc gain less half its bb gain) / 46
#           (gate: +0.15 with the 95% low end above zero; the four losses add up to +0.18 on the
#           first card and +0.58 on the confirm). The card changes nothing: on a PASS a PR writes
#           the entries of the teams whose own gain is above zero into TeamModes.TABLE.
# Each seed is a pair (the arm and aa): 2 x 4 x 24 x 2 = 384 battles, about 25 minutes at 12 workers
# (sizes itself to the host). Every step resumes where it stopped.
# Stop rules on both battle steps (halt; every battle fought is kept and a rerun resumes): 20 failed
# battles (a broken jar), no battle in 30 minutes (a hung step), or 40+ skipped turns a battle over the
# last 100 (the PR #331 build-up). A halt at the very start leaves the whole card unrun (384 battles);
# a halt in ncbb leaves the rest of ncbb plus all 192 of ncxc; in ncxc, the rest of ncxc. No early
# finish on score: the gate pools the four teams.
# The team thread reads claude/pc-team-noconcord-results.
#   ./queue.sh run pc-team-noconcord        (or  .\queue.ps1 run pc-team-noconcord)
# Run it from master (one bench queue at a time):
#   git checkout master && git pull

set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set T = python3 tools/team_modes.py

ncprep | git checkout -q master && V=$(sed -n 's:.*<robot.release>\(.*\)</robot.release>.*:\1:p' ../hadur-robot/pom.xml) && test -n "$V" && rm -f bisect/hadur117.HadurTeam_"$V"aa.jar bisect/hadur117.HadurTeam_"$V"bb.jar bisect/hadur117.HadurTeam_"$V"xc.jar && rm -f ${OUT}/team-noconcord-*.md && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set plans/team-noconcord-set.txt && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && bash ./build-ablation.sh bb && TEAM_MODE_TABLE="$(pwd)/plans/team-noconcord-table.java" TEAM_MODE_SUFFIX=xc bash ./build-ablation.sh tmtab && mkdir -p work && rm -rf work/team-noconcord-"$V"-bb work/team-noconcord-"$V"-xc && for a in bb xc; do sed "s/@V@/$V/g" plans/team-noconcord-$a.args > work/team-noconcord-$a.args || exit 1; done && for j in aa bb xc; do test -f bisect/hadur117.HadurTeam_"$V"$j.jar || exit 1; done && mvn -q compile
ncbb   | mvn -q exec:java "-Dexec.args=@work/team-noconcord-bb.args"
  after: ncprep
  watch: battles=192
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100
ncxc   | mvn -q exec:java "-Dexec.args=@work/team-noconcord-xc.args"
  after: ncbb
  watch: battles=192
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100
ncsum  | ${T} gate --report ${OUT}/team-noconcord-xc.md --control ${OUT}/team-noconcord-bb.md --set plans/team-noconcord-set.txt --seeds 24 --teams 46 --min-aps 0.15 --out-md ${OUT}/team-noconcord-verdict.md
  after: ncxc
ncpr   | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-team-noconcord-results "CONCORD off against the four teams it lost to: fresh-seed confirm" $(ls ${OUT}/team-noconcord-*.md 2>/dev/null)
  after: ncsum
